    {
      "id": "eebj4m3",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2. Governor"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "uxo109p",
      "content": "• The Governor is the constitutional head of the State."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "e5qsodz",
      "content": "• The Governor is appointed by the President of India."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "hk0az6w",
      "content": "• The normal term of office is five years."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "bz25r3v",
      "content": "• The Governor performs executive, legislative, financial and judicial functions."
    },
    {
      "id": "27f2bg9",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "3. Chief Minister"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ju1x4c4",
      "content": "• The Chief Minister is the real executive head of the State Government."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "1d8vhrr",
      "content": "• Appointed by the Governor."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "kiilq6y",
      "content": "• Usually the leader of the majority party in the Legislative Assembly becomes Chief Minister."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "wuj5fgk",
      "content": "• He or she heads the Council of Ministers."
    },
    {
      "id": "0nmsuco",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "4. Council of Ministers"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ivjlzrj",
      "content": "The Council of Ministers assists the Chief Minister in administration."
    },
    {
      "id": "qoqg6kr",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
