    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "fdz8hym",
      "content": "• The State Legislature consists of the Governor and one or two houses."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ew0rey6",
      "content": "• States may have unicameral or bicameral legislature."
    },
    {
      "id": "g2qg1n6",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "6. Legislative Assembly (Vidhan Sabha)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "yu0i7n6",
      "content": "• Lower house of state legislature."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "3eey272",
      "content": "• Members directly elected by people."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "fwm2j12",
      "content": "• Normal term is 5 years."
    },
    {
      "id": "6un5e82",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "7. Legislative Council (Vidhan Parishad)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "1f5pn0g",
      "content": "• Upper house in some states."
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Article 213 empowers the Governor to promulgate ordinances when the state legislature is not in session.",
        "The 6 states with bicameral legislatures are Andhra Pradesh, Telangana, Uttar Pradesh, Bihar, Maharashtra, and Karnataka.",
        "The minimum age required to be appointed as Governor is 35 years.",
        "The Legislative Council (Vidhan Parishad) cannot be dissolved; 1/3rd of its members retire every second year."
      ],
      "id": "pvzuib6"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9iext8n",
      "content": "• It is a permanent body."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "der8odg",
      "content": "• One-third members retire every two years."
    },
    {
